I take a taxi.
The driver is a man.
He smiles and says: 'Good day.'
I say: 'Hello.'
He asks: 'Where are you going?'
I say my new address.
'Welcome to Copenhagen,' he says.
I say: 'Thank you.'
We drive.
He says: 'Copenhagen is a big city.'
'Yes, it is beautiful,' I say.
I look out the window.
I see the streets.
There are tall, beautiful houses.
